SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nFor Oct 1 thru Oct 7\n\nUpcoming **music ev
 ents** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\n\n**A
 ssorted entertainment\, festival & market events may be found here:**\nhtt
 ps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-of-events\n\n**Library programs** 
 may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonpl.libcal.com/\n***Thursday\, October
  1\, 2026***\n***Movie Matinee- Pressure\; 2 PM***\nIn the tense 72 hours 
 before D-Day\, General Dwight D. Eisenhower and Captain James Stagg face a
 n impossible choice- launch the most dangerous seaborne invasion in histor
 y or risk losing the war altogether.\n**Hendersonville Main Library**\nhtt
 ps://hendersonpl.libcal.com/\nhttps://hendersonpl.libcal.com/event/1483431
 0\n\nPumpkin Palooza at The Nix Pumpkin Patch\n**October 3** @ 11:00 am - 
 4:00 pm\; Free\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/pumpkin-palooza-at
 -the-nix-pumpkin-patch\n\n**Sat\; Oct 3rd**\nTRAILSIDE BREWING CO. \\* Ste
 ve Weams Oktoberfest Show \\* 6:00 – 9:00\n\n**Wednesday\, Oct 7th**\nJa
 son DeCristofaro's Jazz Night (Each Wednesday)\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachi
 an Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n\n**Oct 8**\nCroquet & Bocce 
 ball at Jackson Pk\nOct & Nov schedule\nhttps://www.hendersoncountync.gov/
 recreation\n**FYI: Rockin’ on the Rock**\n\nOctober 9\, 2026\n5pm / Free
 \nJump Off Rock\, Laurel Park\, NC\nEnjoy live music at the picturesque Ju
 mp Off Rock\, which overlooks the French Broad River valley and the Blue R
 idge Mountains beyond. Musical offerings ranging from jazz to country\, ro
 ckabilly\, pop\, rock and blues. Organized by the Friends of Laurel Park.\
 nOct 9\; 5:00 pm\; Rockin’ on the Rock with Autumnwood\nJump Off Rock\; 
 4433 Laurel Park Hwy\, Laurel Park\, NC 28739\nhttps://visithendersonville
 nc.org/event/rockin-on-the-rock-with-autumnwood\n\n**October 10**\nBarktob
 er at Booda-fest\; 12:30 pm - 5 pm.\na charity event supporting the local 
 Blue Ridge Humane Society. There will be local vendors with products for y
 ou and your pets and lots of activities for every age. Stein holding conte
 st at 3:00pm and best dressed lederhosen contest at 4:00pm. Bring the pups
  and friends!!\nBoodas brewing\; 120 E Barnwell St\, Hendersonville\,\n\nT
 hese are NOT hosted events and are posted for informational purposes only.
  Please make personal arrangements to meetup with friends and family.\nIf 
 you wish to attend and host one of these events\, I will post the event as
  an individual happening. Hosting only requires being focal point for othe
 rs and making introductions. Simple!!
