SUMMARY:the trails of Jump Off Rock 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A Walk in the Park**\n***Trails of Jump O
 ff Rock\, Laurel Park***\nJump Off Rock offers spectacular scenic mountain
  views and photographic opportunities during all four seasons of the year.
 \nThe forested hiking trials meander below the overlook..\nDifficulty: som
 e short sections of minor challenging footing.\nSuitable for beginners? NO
 \; Moderate steep slopes & occasional challenging footing. Sections of sho
 rt staircases.\nDue to recent events\, Bigfoot discussions are no longer p
 ermitted.\nA Sloth Walking Team event: A casual pace.\n**The Curmudgeon wi
 ll lead this event. Up to 12 ppl** are welcome to join us.\n**https://bigg
 eekdad.com/2015/11/nature-rx/**\nHike Details:\nSocial ‘hour’ at 10:00
  AM. Flotilla leaves at 10:10a\nLength: 0.8 mile RT\; Accum Ascent: 150 ft
 \; Pace: 1.5 mph.\nDrive time: 15 min on a winding\, mountain-climbing bla
 cktop road\nTrlhd: Google Map = “4433 Laurel Park Hwy\, Laurel Park\, NC
 ”\nApprx return time: 12 noon\n**Optional:** Lunch TBD after the walk.\n
 Carpool contributions appreciated. $2.00 suggested\nTHIS IS A DOG-PARTICIP
 ANT WALK. This event is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antic
 s of fun-loving dogs.\nDogs (and Masters) required to be ‘on-leash'. Sma
 ll (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive themselves.\nWeather Check
 : Laurel Park\, NC\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nW
 e currently have 1 driver(s) (=8ppl)\nWe suggest open windows while carpoo
 ling. Only you know your own health status so judge accordingly if an even
 t may endanger your health or the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra
  pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at
  the end of the hike.\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an
  affair.\nAll walks are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN
  safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is 
 a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is
  only to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any outd
 oor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agre
 es to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partn
 ers\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or pe
 rsonal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or whil
 e traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further ag
 rees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow i
 nstructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated f
 rom the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collec
 ted on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's con
 tact: curmudgeonhiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (t
 alk & text)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
