SUMMARY:Pilot Cove/Slate Rock Loop\, the Hike
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nDarlene will host a hike on the Pilot Cove/
 Slate Rock Loop in Pisgah Forest\;\nHidden deep within the Mills River are
 a of Pisgah National Forest\, this trail has rhododendrons and Mtn laurel.
  And\, at the top\, there is a great view from the Forked Ridge Pluton. Pr
 obably the BEST Fall color view.\nAt the Pluton\, we will cajole the frien
 dly resident timber rattler\, Fred.\n**Difficulty:** Rocky with roots with
  a ½ mile very steep uphill section. The return to the cars is on a borin
 g 2-mile section of the gravel Yellow Gap Rd.\n**IF YOU HAVE AN ORANGE VES
 T\; WEAR IT. HUNTING SEASON HAS STARTED. \;-) THEY ARE INEXPENSIVE AT WALM
 ART....**\nWe are the ***HFF Trail Trekkers***: We a’gonna get our step-
 counters a’workin’ !!\nUp to 12 ppl are welcome to join us.\n**PARTICI
 PANTS REQUIRE THE APPROVAL OF THE HIKE ORGANIZER.**\nHike Details:\nSocial
  ‘hour’ at 9:15 am. Tour guide leaves at 9:30 am\nHike Distance: 7 mi 
 Total\; Accum ascent: 1200 ft Pace: 2.0**mph**\n**Drive time: ½ hr\; 12 m
 i 1-way**\n**Return Not earlier than: 2:30pm (=5.0 hrs)**\n**Carpool contr
 ibutions appreciated. $3.00 suggested**\nWeather Check: Brevard\nWAITLISTE
 D PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nWe currently have 1 driver(s) 
 (=??ppl)\nWe suggest slightly open windows while carpooling. Only you know
  your own health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your
  health or the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to a
 void bringing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hik
 e.\nAll hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safet
 y and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is a volu
 nteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only 
 to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor ac
 tivity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to 
 release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, 
 Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal
  loss which might occur while participating in this activity or while trav
 eling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agrees t
 o abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow instruc
 tions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from th
 e group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected on
  this trip for recording on website photo collections.\nDarlene’s contac
 t: (**before** day of hike): 678.428.0858 (text only)\n**Pics: https://www
 .flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
