SUMMARY:Flat Creek Tr & BRPkwy\, a Saunter
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nI am going to the Flat Creek Tr on the Hein
 tooga spur of the BRPkwy\; and **return on the BRPkwy.** Up to 12 of you a
 re welcome to join me.\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend 
 to have pleasant surprises.\nFlat Creek Trail is an amazingly beautiful 2.
 7 mile 1-way hike located just off The Blue Ridge Parkway\, in the Great S
 moky Mountains National Park. The trail follows alongside two different cr
 eeks\, and is full of lush moss\, grass and trees making for an absolutely
  gorgeous and beautiful hike that begins at the Heintooga Picnic area\nWoo
 dlands of red spruce\, American beech\, yellow birch\, and striped and red
  maple make this trail a real treat.\nA bull elk and his family are known 
 to be in this area. We saw them last time!\n**WE WILL RETURN VIA THE BRPKW
 Y** with a few overlook stops. (rest stop at Waterrock Knob).\nDifficulty:
  5 (easy) rockhop Crk Xings. Short steep section at the end.\n**This event
  requires a car shuttle. Sedans acceptable.**\nJohn Muir didn’t like the
  word ‘hike’. “We ought to saunter through them reverently\, not 'hi
 ke' through them.”\nWe are the **Sloth Hike Team of WNC**: “We will ge
 t there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike grou
 ps don’t ***!!***\n**Hike Details:**\n(Social ‘hour’ at 9 AM. Parade
  leaves at 9:10a)\nLength: 3.0 mi total\; Total **descent**: 800 ft: Accum
  ascent: 400 ft\; Elevation: 5000ft\nPace: **1.5mph**\n**We eat\, snack & 
 drink ‘on the go’.**\nDrive time: 60mi/1.75hr (1-way) from Brevard\; v
 ia Hwy 276 thru Maggie Valley.\n**Return trip drive time:** via BRPkwy/Hwy
  215: 85 mi/2.25hrs\n**Return Not earlier than: 4:30PM (=7.5 hrs)**\nTrail
 head: Google Map = “Heintooga Overlook”\nCarpool contributions appreci
 ated. $12.00 suggested (includes parking pass fee)\n**THIS IS NOT A DOG-PA
 RTICIPANT HIKE.** we will be in the GSMNP.\nWeather Check: Waynesville\, N
 C\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 1
  driver(s). (=??ppl)\n**GSMNP Parking Pass reqr’d** (Smoky Mtn Natl Pk P
 arking Tags.doc)\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affa
 ir.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoe
 s into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nWe suggest masks and open
  windows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judge a
 ccordingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of others.\n
 All hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety an
 d adequate equipment.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is a voluntee
 r and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to o
 rganize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activi
 ty. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to rele
 ase from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affi
 liates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal los
 s which might occur while participating in this activity or while travelin
 g in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agrees to ab
 ide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow instruction
 s of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from the gr
 oup.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected on thi
 s trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: curm
 udgeonhiker@gmail.com\n(**BEFORE** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text
 )\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
